WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.480
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.650
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:34.260
Rin Rin and Mei Mei's 
Super Exciting Plan.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.320
I wonder if there's 
anything fun to do.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:49.000
I wonder if I'll get another 
postcard from Mr. Full-Time.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.910
You just got one the other day.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.860
Hey, Mr. Handa. Entertain me.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:01.100
You're my caretaker, right?

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:04.420
I'm not your caretaker. 
I'm a zoo keeper.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.470
Oh, who cares?

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:09.060
Tell me an interesting story.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.420
An interesting story?

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:12.520
Oh!

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.680
Want to see the stone I found 
by the river the other day?

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.340
It's very smooth!

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.270
Is that interesting?

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:22.530
Then, yesterday, the supermarket 
had a great dea—

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:24.500
Forget it.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:25.540
What?

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.170
Prince Han is dreamy today, too.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:35.050
Huh?

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:36.850
Rin Rin?

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:38.780
Mei Mei?

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.930
So, what were you doing back there?

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:47.390
Well, you see...

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.140
I'm really sorry!

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.560
But could you not come near the 
Panda Corner for a while?

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:56.900
Panda asked me to tell you that.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.570
He said I was too distracting 
and he couldn't do his work.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.410
My brother's trying to 
act all sensitive.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.980
He's just a lazy bum.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:09.000
That's not true, Mei Mei!

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:10.790
Take a look at this.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.930
Look how cute he is!

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:15.690
And look at this!

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.010
He fell asleep while playing.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.680
And over here, he fell asleep 
while eating bamboo.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.700
Oh, he's too cute!

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.090
You see it now, right?

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:29.420
Panda isn't just some lazy bum,

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:31.000
he's a cute, lazy bum.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.900
So you'll admit to the 
lazy bum part...

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:36.510
What were you doing there, Mei Mei?

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.200
I was admiring...

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:42.950
Prince Han from afar.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.690
Are you talking about Mr. Handa?

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:46.830
Prince H-a-n!

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.220
He's my prince!

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:53.400
I'm having my brother 
take pictures of him.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.060
Look!

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:56.430
Isn't he dreamy?

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:59.340
See? He looks so round and cool!

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:00.810
That smile!

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.470
His eyes are so slanted and his 
face is so chubby, I die!

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:06.550
Panda is so cute in this picture!

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:08.360
I'll send it to you if you want.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.890
Really?! Then I'll send 
you the pictures I have

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.480
with Mr. Handa, as well.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:24.680
Prince Han!

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:25.700
Panda!

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:31.700
I wish there was some way I 
could look at Panda all day.

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.840
I know! How about the four 
of us go somewhere?

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:38.040
What?! With Prince Han?!

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.050
Oh, it's okay.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.670
It's plenty just for me to 
admire him from afar.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:43.070
Are you sure about that?

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:44.670
Yes...

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.810
It's not good to hold things in.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.440
You promise you won't tell anyone?

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:50.670
Of course!

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:52.620
Well...

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:56.850
I was thinking it'd be great 
if I could get his autograph!

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.910
An autograph? From Mr. Handa?

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.070
In his own handwriting, if possible!

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.070
Handa

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:05.530
Then why don't you get 
one when we all go out?

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.530
But isn't that being 
a little presumptuous?

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:09.910
Not at all!

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:14.720
I'll invite Mr. Handa, 
so make sure you invite Panda.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:17.260
What am I going to do?

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.710
Oh, Mr. Handa!

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:28.230
Would you like to go somewhere 
on your next day off?

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:31.510
Huh? With me? 
What brought this on?

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:33.260
I actually know a girl

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:36.010
who'd like to get to know you better.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:37.940
Who is it?

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:41.130
It's gotta be Miss Sasako!

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.080
Huh?! Wh-Why?!

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:47.300
Well, she's the only girl you know.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:48.660
I know a few others...

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.600
Like um...

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.620
You don't, do you?

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:55.250
You can't let this chance pass you by!

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.820
You like Miss Sasako, right?

00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:59.330
Yeah, but...

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.250
Hey! How do you know that?

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:03.760
What? Everyone knows that.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:05.380
Really?! Who's everyone?

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:08.870
Well, there's Mr. Llama, 
Mandrill, Anteater,

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:10.720
and even Mr. Red River Hog.

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:13.190
Even Mr. Red River Hog?!

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:17.580
All right, that's a yes. 
Please look after him.

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:22.190
Thank goodness. I'll contact 
you with the details later.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:24.650
Panda

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:24.650
Hey, big brother,

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.720
would you like to go somewhere 
on your next day off?

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:30.370
With just you?

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:32.210
No, there'd be four of us.

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:33.390
Who else?

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:34.370
Um...

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:38.960
A couple fans! They're huge fans of yours.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.540
What? Fans?

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:45.270
Fans, eh? Looks like I 
have no other choice.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:52.760
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:01.690
<i>My next day off...</i>

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:04.320
My next day off, huh?

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:07.180
Wh-What, Panda?

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:11.700
I'm going to go hang out 
with some fans of mine.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:12.840
Oh.

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:14.370
Are you jealous?

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.080
Not at all!

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:20.510
I wonder how they'll entertain me.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:25.660
Eat lots and lots!

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:28.630
You're so cute when you're 
eating bamboo, Mr. Panda!

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:34.440
He seems so happy.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:37.600
But on my next day off...

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:41.810
Look, Miss Sasako! 
It's so smooth!

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:45.310
Look, Mr. Handa! 
This one is, too!

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:47.240
So smooth!

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.440
So smooth!

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:49.780
So smooth!

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:54.740
Hehehe

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:00.510
Miss Sasako... what is that?

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:05.010
I thought it might be

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:08.050
a good idea to wear these 
glasses when I'm angry.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:12.380
People tell me that I still 
smile when I'm mad, so...

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:13.890
Are you mad right now?

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:14.560
Not at all.

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.650
Could you take those off, then?

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:20.150
You look pretty scary.

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:23.010
What? But I really like them...

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:25.480
You'll scare any customers 
that come in.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:26.320
Right?

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.850
I'd like to scare some customers,

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:30.540
so could you bring some in for me?

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:35.950
Just because things are quiet,
 don't try to get me to go bring people in.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:39.790
The plan is all set.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:43.250
We just have to think of 
the perfect situation.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:46.710
We have to make it a wonderful day.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.220
Popular Shops
 You Should Know

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.220
Arune!

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:00.220
Special

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:00.220
Day Trip 
Planning

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:15.650
Panda

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:15.650
It's finally tomorrow, Rin Rin!

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:17.200
Are you all ready?

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:20.040
Well, actually...

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.060
Will you help me decide?

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.770
I should probably get 
an autograph board signed.

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:29.040
But there's my favorite 
handkerchief, too...

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:31.040
Oh, I know!

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:35.130
It'd be amazing to have 
him sign this, too.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:38.600
Oh, I don't know what to do!

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:40.420
Why don't you get them all signed?

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:41.930
What?! All of them?

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.960
Oh, I couldn't do that!

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:48.460
But maybe I do want them.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:53.070
All right. 
See you tomorrow.

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:57.490
Oh, Mei Mei, you're so excited.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:09:59.480
I know!

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:03.040
What if we took some commemorative 
pictures at a portrait studio?

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:06.640
I could wear a suit, 
in a Gothic setting.

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:09.920
Wait.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:13.820
I could also go twinsies with Panda.

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:18.020
I can't choose!

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:19.300
They're both so amazing!

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:21.850
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:21.240
Oh, that's good, too!

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:22.360
And that, too!

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:24.350
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:29.230
I got too excited.

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:33.650
What do you mean
 you can't make it?

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:36.650
I'm sorry. I have a fever.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:39.820
If it's a cold, I wouldn't want you to catch it,

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.670
so you three go on and have fun.

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:43.620
But...

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:46.080
Panda's Weekend

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:46.080
Ueno

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:46.080
Oh, and for lunch,

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:49.310
you guys should go to a place 
called Grilled Bamboo.

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.750
I'll text you a coupon in a bit.

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:54.570
Do your best, Mei Mei.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:56.260
Rin Rin!

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:58.220
Are you ready to go?

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:00.370
Oh, yeah...

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:05.470
I bet everyone's having fun...

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:10.540
Rintaro Hayashi's biggest regret.

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:13.700
Huh?

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:21.150
Yes?

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:24.570
Mei Mei!

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:25.890
Why are you...

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:27.440
Don't worry about it.

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:30.560
How's your fever? 
Come on, you should be laying down.

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:33.580
Strictly

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:33.580
Pudding

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.580
All you 
need for 
your fever!

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:39.460
Thanks for visiting, Mei Mei.

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:40.210
If you leave now—

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:40.880
Nope.

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:44.800
I know how you feel better 
than anyone else.

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:47.810
I couldn't go have fun just by myself.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:49.360
I'm sorry.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:50.600
Oh, stop worrying about it.

00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:53.370
Here you go. Have some rice porridge.

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:54.770
Hey, it's a panda.

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:56.810
Come on, eat up.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.080
It's too cute to eat!

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:02.380
Come on! Eat! Eat!

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:04.300
All right. Thank you for the food.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:09.340
Did you draw the 
face with chocolate?

00:12:09.340 --> 00:12:10.160
I did!

00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:12.390
I see...

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:16.750
How is it?

00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:23.250
Thank you.

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:30.710
Once you're feeling better,
let's plan another outing.

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:34.520
We'll have a great time.

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:36.040
Of course!

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:38.860
I'm going to get Prince Han's 
autograph, no matter what!

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:42.070
Oh, I said it! 
How embarrassing!

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:46.200
When did I become so bold?

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:53.410
Exciting Shiny Land

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:53.410
Entrance

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:49.900
Um, Panda? Huh?

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:52.730
You're so reserved, Mr. Handa.

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:53.410
Huh?

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:56.870
If you like me so much, 
you should just say so.

00:12:56.870 --> 00:12:57.630
What?!

00:12:58.360 --> 00:13:01.590
So you were one of my 
fans, Mr. Handa...

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:03.270
Do you want my autograph?

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:04.760
Um... Where's Miss Sasako?

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:10.480
It's so slow today.

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:11.800
Indeed. Very slow.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:16.180
Could you stop wearing those 
glasses whenever it's slow?

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:21.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:20.790
Smelt Fishing.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:23.520
Welcome...

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:26.110
to my hometown, the North Pole!

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:28.620
Like hell it's the North Pole.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:31.430
This is very much Japan!

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:34.060
Can't you dream, Grizzly?

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:36.290
If you want me to dream, 
then let me sleep!

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.770
Thank you for driving us up here,

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:41.340
even though you're in the 
middle of hibernating.

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:45.460
Yeah, well, we're here now.

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:47.260
Come on, let's get this show on the road.

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.390
And now we will commence

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:57.790
the first annual smelt 
fishing competition.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:00.760
Whoever gets the most gets a prize.

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:02.150
Prize!

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:06.130
I'll be sleeping in the car. 
Call me when you're done.

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:09.200
I'm gonna sleep, too!

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:11.660
You stay here and fish smelts.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.120
What?

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:15.960
Then give me the prize.

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:17.790
If you get the most.

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:23.370
The prize is as good as mine.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.160
You seem very confident.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:27.810
Did you forget who I am?

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:29.040
A show-off?

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:32.070
No! I'm Penguin! Pen-guin!

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:35.220
If I get serious, there 
won't be an end...

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:40.440
to the fish I catch!

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:46.020
I don't think I want to eat any 
smelts you catch like that.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:47.630
I'm not sure about that, either.

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:49.370
Huh? Why not?

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:54.950
So, how many years do you 
get for baiting smelts?

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:56.990
This has nothing to do 
with that kind of "bait,"

00:14:56.990 --> 00:14:59.670
so I'm just going to omit 
an explanation, okay?

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.420
I wonder where would be best?

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.350
Mr. Penguin,

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:08.740
it's times like this you should 
use your famous sophistry.

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:11.660
I think by that, you mean my 
vast sophistication.

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:14.930
But I actually don't know that 
much about smelt fishing.

00:15:15.590 --> 00:15:20.030
It's so like you to be
of no use at all, Mr. Penguin.

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:23.990
I don't need that kind of likeness!

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:26.420
How about we look it 
up on the Internet?

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:27.810
Oh, good idea.

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:29.250
Let's see.

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:32.400
"The route that smelt swim

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:36.130
is rather predictable, so as soon 
as that place is found,

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:37.580
even beginners can catch a lot.

00:15:38.150 --> 00:15:42.950
Smelt tend to follow the 
current of the lake.

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:45.700
So at the point where the 
current changes direction,

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:48.650
fish will tend to gather, so it's 
a great thing to look out for."

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:48.800
Standing Tent

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:53.510
Standing Tent

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:50.510
So, somewhere like this.

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:53.510
If you already know, 
don't have me look it up!

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:08.090
"The trick to fishing smelt, 
is to lure the fish by wiggling the line.

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:11.240
And then stopping now and then."

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:15.930
Oh, it says that five 
seconds is enough.

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:17.580
Start moving again, everyone!

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:22.850
"Move the line up and down to 
attract the fish to the bait.

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:26.170
Check your surroundings to determine 
the range and rhythm of the movement."

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:29.180
Wiggle, wiggle, stop!

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:31.160
Wiggle, wiggle, stop!

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:33.560
I don't seem to be having any luck.

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:36.000
I think it's because 
Mr. Penguin is being too noisy.

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:38.720
Then I'll go get them myself!

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:41.720
I'm sorry, could you not do that?

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:43.730
I've got a big haul!

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.830
Those aren't smelt.

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:49.220
Did you find a bamboo thicket, Panda?

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:52.900
Yeah. The bamboo here is really good.

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:55.600
Let's stop fishing,

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:58.370
and change this into a 
bamboo fetching contest.

00:16:58.940 --> 00:17:00.360
Start!

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:03.260
How about I change it 
to we don't change it.

00:17:03.260 --> 00:17:05.380
Oh, by the way,

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.040
I have some smelt, too.

00:17:08.530 --> 00:17:10.210
Where'd you get those?

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:12.690
On my way to get bamboo,

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:15.010
there were some people
 who had caught a bunch.

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:17.970
Wow.

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:20.710
You caught so many.

00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:22.280
That's so cool.

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:24.150
I'm jealous.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.430
Would you like some?

00:17:26.430 --> 00:17:27.980
Thanks!

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:30.470
That's rather shameless.

00:17:30.470 --> 00:17:32.610
I'm glad they were nice people.

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:35.030
I'm going to do a lap 
around the lake, too.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:36.720
How about you fish?

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:00.540
Oh! I might have caught one!

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:01.520
What should I do?

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:03.710
Pull, pull! But slowly.

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:09.190
Yay!

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:11.650
But that's finally our first one.

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:13.600
One would be enough for one bite.

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:16.340
Smelts are pretty small.

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:17.150
For now.

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:20.190
Do they get any bigger?

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:21.620
Smelts...

00:18:22.220 --> 00:18:24.790
Master of the Lake: Giant Catfish

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:29.120
are the biggest when they're young.

00:18:27.060 --> 00:18:29.500
Young 
Smelt

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:33.830
And then as they mature, they divide.

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:37.300
Once there are enough 
to be considered a school,

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:39.760
they're about this size.

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:42.880
Wow! That's amazing!

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:45.230
So since you're so big, Polar Bear,

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:47.150
does that mean you'll 
shrink one day, too?

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:50.270
Yep. I'll be my own herd.

00:18:50.930 --> 00:18:53.060
All right, everyone gather 
around <i>(shuugou)</i>.

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:54.930
Fifteen <i>(juugo)</i>.

00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:56.030
Fad <i>(ryuukou)</i>.

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:58.370
Hugo.

00:18:58.760 --> 00:19:00.740
That's enough. Let's fish.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:11.130
No luck at all here.

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:14.400
Well, you aren't even fishing.

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:17.920
I think I'm gonna go sleep 
in the car after all.

00:19:19.030 --> 00:19:20.130
This seems hopeless.

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:22.220
Then I'll—

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:24.340
That's quite all right.

00:19:24.340 --> 00:19:25.570
Oh. I see.

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:26.470
I know!

00:19:27.670 --> 00:19:28.760
Did you think of a good idea—

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:31.150
Big winner!

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:37.100
A snowball fight?

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:39.290
All right!

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:43.840
Take that!

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:52.750
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:54.670
Take that!

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.380
Here we go. Here we go.

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:02.840
Here we go!

00:20:03.350 --> 00:20:05.190
Hold it right there!

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:13.270
Take that!

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:22.150
What the hell happened to fishing?

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:26.500
We sort of forgot our original motive.

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:27.910
So did you catch anything?

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:29.950
Well...

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:36.960
The hell did we come all 
the way up here for?

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:39.130
You guys are hopeless, damn it.

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:43.050
Wow, you caught a lot.

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:45.990
It certainly is a big catch!

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:48.090
There best times 
for catching smelt

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:50.250
are just before sunrise 
and just after sunset.

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.950
So timing has a lot to do with it.

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:54.650
Wow, that's impressive.

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:57.470
If you're satisfied, 
we're heading home.

00:20:57.470 --> 00:21:00.210
By the way, where did 
Mr. Polar Bear...

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:03.910
The hell is that?

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:07.990
Welcome.

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:15.710
So warm.

00:21:16.360 --> 00:21:18.070
This is amazing.

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:19.880
A café made of ice.

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:22.780
By the way, what's the 
prize for smelt fishing?

00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:27.180
We all got some, so everyone 
will be getting the prize.

00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:29.460
All right, here you go.

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:32.780
A dish made from smelts.

00:21:32.780 --> 00:21:34.550
I have a pizza baking right now, too.

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:36.600
That smells good.

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:39.320
We'd like two coffees, please.

00:21:40.590 --> 00:21:41.600
Um...

00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:43.280
Welcome.

00:21:46.850 --> 00:21:48.390
There's been an addition to an order.

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:50.910
Please make pasta with these smelts.

00:21:58.110 --> 00:22:00.210
Hey! The fried 
fish is coming up!

00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:02.940
Yes, yes, yes.

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:07.400
I'd like more bamboo 
grass, Mr. Waiter!

00:22:07.400 --> 00:22:09.680
I'm usually on that side, too!

00:22:11.090 --> 00:22:13.450
Two more customers coming in!

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:17.470
Welcome to the off-site 
Polar Bear's Café!

00:22:17.850 --> 00:22:21.440
Hey, Mr. Penguin, 
where are my seconds?

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:24.150
Hey! You should be 
helping, too, Panda!

00:23:54.870 --> 00:24:24.830
Next Time

00:23:56.680 --> 00:23:58.370
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:58.370 --> 00:23:59.640
What is it, Panda?

00:23:59.640 --> 00:24:03.830
When are the times you want to 
refer to me as Master Panda?

00:24:03.830 --> 00:24:05.160
When?

00:24:05.160 --> 00:24:06.380
Generally, never.

00:24:06.380 --> 00:24:07.710
How about Prince Pan—

00:24:07.710 --> 00:24:08.510
Never.

00:24:08.510 --> 00:24:09.300
Um,

00:24:09.300 --> 00:24:12.760
what's that smell when 
you open import CDs?

00:24:12.760 --> 00:24:14.540
Miss Sasako, too sudden.

00:24:14.540 --> 00:24:16.980
We didn't say a single word about CDs.

00:24:16.980 --> 00:24:18.500
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:18.500 --> 00:24:20.340
Next week's Polar Bear Café

00:24:20.340 --> 00:24:22.350
will be brought to you 
using real animal voices.

00:24:22.350 --> 00:24:23.360
It'll be with humans.

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:24.560
Doll Festival
The Animal Doctor

00:24:23.360 --> 00:24:24.560
Enjoy!
